@@ -993,6 +993,18 @@ def TensorIR_MatmulOp : TensorIR_Op<"matmul", [
     * right_triangle: Same choices and zero-input promise as left_triangle,
       applied to B's logical innermost [K, N] dimensions. Both parameters
       may be set; the K loop uses the intersection of their allowed ranges.
+    * input_precision: Optional `#nv_tensor_ir.input_precision<ieee>` (the
+      default) or `#nv_tensor_ir.input_precision<tf32>`. Controls how f32
+      inputs use tensor cores. Only f32 matmuls (f32 `A`, `B`, and `C`) may
+      use `tf32`; other element types must use `ieee`, which has no effect
+      on them.
+      - `ieee`: f32 operands are multiplied at full f32 precision. Tensor
+        cores do not support this, so the current backend computes the
+        product with FMA instructions, which is much slower.
+      - `tf32`: both `A` and `B` are rounded to tf32 (round-to-nearest-even)
+        before the multiply, so the product can run on tensor cores. The
+        accumulator and result stay f32. This trades input precision for
+        throughput.
 
     The numerical semantics follow CUDA Tile matrix-multiply-accumulate
     operations (`mmaf` and `mmai`) for their supported type combinations.
